## A shift caused by insertion

```go
type Status int

const (
    Pending Status = iota // 0
    Paused                // newly inserted: 1
    Ready                 // changed from 1 to 2
)
```

If a database already stores `1` for `Ready`, the new program will read that old row as `Paused`.

## Stable alternative

```go
const (
    Pending Status = 0
    Ready   Status = 1
    Paused  Status = 2
)
```

## Protect the values

```go
func TestStableStatusValues(t *testing.T) {
    tests := []struct {
        name string
        got  Status
        want Status
    }{
        {"pending", Pending, 0},
        {"ready", Ready, 1},
        {"paused", Paused, 2},
    }

    for _, tt := range tests {
        if tt.got != tt.want {
            t.Errorf("%s: got %d, want %d", tt.name, tt.got, tt.want)
        }
    }
}
```

The test turns the numeric mapping into an explicit contract. A future reorder fails during development instead of silently corrupting meaning in production.
